---
import GuideLayout from '../../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
const toc=[{href:'#overview',label:'Overview'},{href:'#how-it-works',label:'How It Works'},{href:'#categories',label:'Categories'},{href:'#obtaining-items',label:'Obtaining Items'},{href:'#recommended',label:'Recommended Early Collections'},{href:'#mistakes',label:'Common Mistakes'},{href:'#related',label:'Related Guides'}];
---
<GuideLayout title="Collections | L2 Guardian Guides" lang="en" active="collections" toc={toc}><div class="content"><a class="back" href="/en/">← Back to home</a>

    <section class="hero no-image">

     

      <div class="hero-body">
        <div class="badge">GUARDIAN SYSTEM</div>

        <h1>Collections</h1>

        <p class="subtitle">
          Collections are permanent, shared across the account stat bonuses you unlock by registering specific sets of
          items. They apply to every character on your account, so time spent completing them is never wasted,
          even if you switch or reroll a class later.
        </p>

        <div class="info-grid">
          <div class="info-card">
            <div class="label">System Type</div>
            <div class="value">Permanent / Shared across the account</div>
          </div>

          <div class="info-card">
            <div class="label">Best For</div>
            <div class="value">All Classes</div>
          </div>

          <div class="info-card">
            <div class="label">Difficulty</div>
            <div class="value">Low / Medium</div>
          </div>

          <div class="info-card">
            <div class="label">Priority</div>
            <div class="value">Medium to High</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
	
	
	<section class="section quick-start">
  <div class="quick-head">
    <div class="quick-icon">⚡</div>
    <div>
      <h2>Quick Start</h2>
      <p>What to know before opening the Collections window for the first time.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="quick-grid">

    <div class="quick-card">
      <div class="quick-title">Scope</div>
      <div class="quick-value">Shared across the account</div>
      <span class="quick-tag high">High Priority</span>
    </div>

    <div class="quick-card">
      <div class="quick-title">Categories</div>
      <div class="quick-value">8 Tabs</div>
      <span class="quick-tag medium">Medium Priority</span>
    </div>

    <div class="quick-card">
      <div class="quick-title">Main Source</div>
      <div class="quick-value">Random Craft</div>
      <span class="quick-tag high">High Priority</span>
    </div>

    <div class="quick-card">
      <div class="quick-title">Items Used</div>
      <div class="quick-value">Consumed Forever</div>
      <span class="quick-tag high">High Priority</span>
    </div>

  </div>

  <div class="quick-footer">

    <div class="quick-tip">
      <strong>Items are consumed</strong>
      Once an item is registered into a collection it is removed from your inventory permanently, so double check before confirming.
    </div>

    <div class="quick-tip">
      <strong>Sealed items count too</strong>
      Most collection items have a Sealed equivalent obtainable through Random Craft, you rarely need to buy or farm the unsealed version.
    </div>

    <div class="quick-tip">
      <strong>Shared across the account, not per character</strong>
      Progress and completed collections carry over to every character you create on the same account.
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

    <section class="section" id="overview">
      <h2>Overview</h2>

      <p>
        Collections are sets of specific items that, once fully registered, grant a permanent stat bonus.
        They are available from level 1, and both their progress and their effects are shared across every
        character on your account, though not between different servers.
      </p>
	<img
	  src="/images/collections.png"
	  alt="Collections window in Lineage 2 Guardian"
	  class="guide-image-small"/>
      <div class="note">
        <strong>Recommendation:</strong> Open the Collections window early and check the search option to see
        if any item you already own can be registered, some early gear pieces qualify without you realizing it.
      </div>
	 
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="how-it-works">
      <h2>How It Works</h2>

      <div class="steps">

        <div class="step">
          <div class="num">1</div>
          <div>
            <strong>Register an item</strong>
            <p>Select the item with left click, then open the Collections button from your inventory. Any collection that item can fill will be highlighted.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="num">2</div>
          <div>
            <strong>Item is consumed</strong>
            <p>Once added, the item is permanently removed from your inventory. It cannot be taken back out, so make sure you are not going to need it equipped.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="num">3</div>
          <div>
            <strong>Use alternative slots when available</strong>
            <p>Some collections accept more than one valid item per slot (for example a normal spellbook or its Sealed version). You can freely mix which version you use for each slot as long as the total required count is met.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="num">4</div>
          <div>
            <strong>Effect applies immediately</strong>
            <p>As soon as the last required item is registered, the collection completes and its bonus is applied right away, permanent bonuses stay active forever, temporary ones show their expiration in the Collections screen.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="warning">
        <strong>Some items cannot be registered.</strong>
        Augmented items, enchanted items (unless stated otherwise), items with inserted Soul Crystals, most unsealable Sealed items and equipped items cannot be added to a collection.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="categories">
      <h2>Categories</h2>

      <p>
        Collections are split into 8 tabs. Hover any category inside the game to see your completion percentage for it,
        and use Favorites to keep the collections you are actively working on at the top of the list.
      </p>

      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Category</th>
            <th>Focus</th>
            <th>Example Collection</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>

        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Attack</strong></td>
            <td>P./M. Atk., Skill Power, Critical Rate/Damage</td>
            <td>Ambidexterity: P./M. Atk. +125</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Defense</strong></td>
            <td>P./M. Def., Received damage/critical reduction</td>
            <td>Great Power: P./M. Def. +100</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Support</strong></td>
            <td>Max HP/MP/CP, Casting/Atk. Speed, Cooldown</td>
            <td>Music Lover I: Max MP +150</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Special</strong></td>
            <td>Resistances (Pull, Hold, Suppression, Imprisonment...)</td>
            <td>Undying Body III: Hellfire Resistance +3%</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Stats</strong></td>
            <td>Raw STR/DEX/CON/INT/WIT/MEN</td>
            <td>Resistance Set: STR/INT/DEX/WIT +1</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Utility</strong></td>
            <td>Sayha's Grace, XP/SP gain, inventory/warehouse slots</td>
            <td>Supporting Accessories I: Acquired XP/SP +2%</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Events</strong></td>
            <td>Temporary collections tied to specific offers</td>
            <td>Growth Rune Collection II: Acquired XP/SP +2%</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Favorites</strong></td>
            <td>Not a real category, a pinboard for any collection you star</td>
            <td>Not applicable</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="obtaining-items">
      <h2>Obtaining Items</h2>

      <p>
        In Guardian, Random Craft is the main source of items to complete collections, this is the intended
        path from early game instead of a later progression bonus.
		<br>Most collection items have a Sealed equivalent that can drop from Random Craft, so you rarely
		need to farm or buy the raw unsealed version.
      </p>

      <div class="note">
        <strong>Recommendation:</strong> Save low grade items you would otherwise sell, many of them are valid
        Random Craft materials and feed directly into collection progress.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="recommended">
      <h2>Recommended Early Collections</h2>

      <p>
        This section will list the cheapest and most efficient collections to complete during your first days
        on Guardian, based on real inside the game costs rather than theoretical ones.
      </p>

      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Collection</th>
            <th>Required Items</th>
            <th>Effect</th>
            <th>Why Early</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>

        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="4">To be filled in.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="note">
        <strong>Note:</strong> This table is a placeholder, fill it in with the collections that are actually
        cheap and worth prioritizing on Guardian.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="mistakes">
      <h2>Common Mistakes</h2>

      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Mistake</th>
            <th>Impact</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>

        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Selling low grade items instead of checking Random Craft/collection value first</td>
            <td class="bad">High</td>
          </tr>

          <tr>
            <td>Registering an item without checking if you need it equipped first</td>
            <td class="bad">High</td>
          </tr>

          <tr>
            <td>Ignoring Utility and Support collections in favor of only Attack ones</td>
            <td class="bad">Medium</td>
          </tr>

          <tr>
            <td>Not using the Favorites tab to track active collections</td>
            <td>Low</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="note">
        <strong>Best practice:</strong> Before selling or disenchanting anything, check whether it has a
        collection mark on its icon, it is an easy way to avoid losing free permanent stats.
      </div>
    </section>

